WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.800
Good morning, Hank. It's Tuesday.

00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:03.720
First things first, Hank, you are a dad!

00:00:03.729 --> 00:00:07.949
Katherine had a baby boy over the weekend;
his name is Orin, he is adorable and I

00:00:07.949 --> 00:00:09.649
am SO SO HAPPY.

00:00:09.649 --> 00:00:13.189
My excitement about this baby is at the level
of, like, Cheez Doodles guy.

00:00:13.189 --> 00:00:17.969
Yaaaaa!!!!!!

00:00:17.969 --> 00:00:21.269
This also means that Hank is really
and truly on paternity leave now, but fear

00:00:21.269 --> 00:00:25.600
not; in the coming weeks we will have several
excellent Guest Hanks, beginning this Friday

00:00:25.610 --> 00:00:27.410
with NerdyandQuirky Sabrina.

00:00:27.410 --> 00:00:31.740
Second things second, next month will be the
10th annual Project for Awesome—wait is

00:00:31.750 --> 00:00:33.079
that possibly correct?

00:00:33.079 --> 00:00:35.199
Oh my God I'm old; I’m super old.

00:00:35.200 --> 00:00:36.300
When did I become old?

00:00:36.309 --> 00:00:39.879
It was this weekend, when my baby brother
had a baby.

00:00:39.879 --> 00:00:43.600
I've gone from Cheez Doodles guy excited to
glimpsing the void in less than a minute;

00:00:43.600 --> 00:00:46.920
but right the 10th Annual Project for Awesome
(no need to fear how old you’ve become)

00:00:46.920 --> 00:00:51.480
will begin at noon eastern time on December
9th, and we need your help in a couple ways.

00:00:51.480 --> 00:00:55.920
First, though, some background: The Project
for Awesome started in 2007, when Nerdfighteria

00:00:55.920 --> 00:00:59.720
essentially tricked YouTube's algorithm into
featuring videos about charity.

00:00:59.720 --> 00:01:03.080
Over the years, the Project for Awesome has
evolved a lot, but it's always been focused

00:01:03.080 --> 00:01:06.360
on 1. decreasing the overall level of suck in the
world, and 2.

00:01:06.360 --> 00:01:09.500
encouraging people to make great videos about
their favorite charities.

00:01:09.500 --> 00:01:10.780
So here's how it's gonna work this year:

00:01:10.780 --> 00:01:14.420
First, hopefully many of you will make Project
for Awesome videos: The idea here is that

00:01:14.430 --> 00:01:17.909
on December 9th, you upload a video about
a charity you care about.

00:01:17.909 --> 00:01:22.130
You explain why the work they do is so important
and how they do it well, and then you encourage

00:01:22.130 --> 00:01:25.600
people to vote for your video at projectforawesome.com.

00:01:25.600 --> 00:01:28.859
This is a great way to spread the word about
your favorite charities, and also the charities

00:01:28.859 --> 00:01:31.039
that receive the most votes will get grants.

00:01:31.040 --> 00:01:34.720
Last year, the top-voted charities received
$25,000 a piece.

00:01:34.720 --> 00:01:38.840
Then there is the live show: So, for 48 hours
straight, beginning at noon eastern time on

00:01:38.840 --> 00:01:43.159
December 9th, there will be a continuous
livestream here at the vlogbrothers channel

00:01:43.159 --> 00:01:46.000
hosted by Hank and me and lots of special
guests.

00:01:46.000 --> 00:01:49.030
In the livestream, we'll be highlighting our
favorite Project for Awesome videos, probably

00:01:49.030 --> 00:01:52.590
covering our faces in peanut butter, and also
raising money for charity.

00:01:52.590 --> 00:01:55.940
There will be an Indiegogo with lots of great
perks from all kinds of amazing YouTubers,

00:01:55.950 --> 00:02:00.610
and all the proceeds will go to Nerdfighteria's
charity, The Foundation to Decrease Worldsuck,

00:02:00.610 --> 00:02:04.539
which I know doesn't sound like a real charity,
but I promise it is one.

00:02:04.539 --> 00:02:09.510
It is a federally sanctioned 501(c)3 organization,
and yes, your donations are tax deductible

00:02:09.510 --> 00:02:13.290
if you live in the United States, and possibly
if you don’t, but I don't know your tax laws.

00:02:13.290 --> 00:02:17.400
Right, okay, so the Foundation to Decrease
Worldsuck has no overhead because everyone

00:02:17.400 --> 00:02:21.630
who works for it volunteers their time, which
means that 100% of donations, lest the cost

00:02:21.630 --> 00:02:24.230
of producing and shipping physical perks,
goes to charity.

00:02:24.230 --> 00:02:26.700
Over the last three years, we’ve raised
more than $3,000,000.

00:02:26.700 --> 00:02:28.120
How do we choose the charities?

00:02:28.130 --> 00:02:31.950
Well, during the first half of the project
for awesome, we raise money for pre-selected charities.

00:02:31.950 --> 00:02:34.950
This year, they will be Save the Children
and Partners in Health.

00:02:34.950 --> 00:02:39.110
These are both great organizations our community
has worked with for a long time.

00:02:39.110 --> 00:02:42.600
And we've seen the impact that our donations
to Partners in Health and Save the Children

00:02:42.610 --> 00:02:48.410
can have, from Bangladesh to Haiti to Ethiopia
to the United Sates to refugee camps in Jordan.

00:02:48.410 --> 00:02:52.160
Pre-selecting charities also allows us to
gather matching donations, which means that

00:02:52.160 --> 00:02:56.540
for the first half of the Project for Awesome,
every dollar you donate will be worth as at least $2.

00:02:56.540 --> 00:03:00.760
Which reminds me: If you happen to be a person
who wants to make a very large donation to

00:03:00.760 --> 00:03:07.340
this year’s Project for Awesome—say, anything
over $1,000—please email me at hankandjohn@gmail.com

00:03:07.340 --> 00:03:09.400
with the subject line "Matching."

00:03:09.400 --> 00:03:13.340
We will add your donations to the matching
fund and thank you profusely, and to reiterate:

00:03:13.340 --> 00:03:15.060
Your donations are tax deductible.

00:03:15.070 --> 00:03:18.380
Okay so then during the second half of the
Project for Awesome, we'll raise money for

00:03:18.380 --> 00:03:23.860
charities chosen by you, the nerdfighter community,
via voting at projectforawesome.com.

00:03:23.860 --> 00:03:28.740
Last year, winning charities ranged from water.org
to the American Association for Suicide Prevention.

00:03:28.740 --> 00:03:33.480
It's up to you to decide what charities to make videos
about and which to support with your votes.

00:03:33.480 --> 00:03:35.900
So here's what we could use from you right now
in comments:

00:03:35.900 --> 00:03:37.360
One, perk ideas.

00:03:37.360 --> 00:03:40.640
What perks would get you excited about donating
to this year's Project for Awesome?

00:03:40.640 --> 00:03:42.480
Or, what perks have you loved in the past?

00:03:42.490 --> 00:03:44.950
And number two, guest suggestions.

00:03:44.950 --> 00:03:48.280
Are there people you would love to see on
the Project for Awesome livestream?

00:03:48.290 --> 00:03:50.000
If so, let us know in comments.

00:03:50.000 --> 00:03:53.740
Hank, congratulations congratulations congratulations!

00:03:53.740 --> 00:03:59.000
I will not see you on Friday, but it’s okay—I
will see Sabrina, and you have a baby!

